                    <chunk name="param_input" index="8">
                      <items count="6">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Total rainfall depth (mm) the piped drainage is assumed to carry off this storm, so it never reaches the surface. Usually the depth of the storm the sewers were designed for, read off the same rainfall statistics (the source study uses the 2-year, 24-hour depth). It comes off after the climate allowance, in proportion from every block: each is scaled by 1 − drainage/total, and a storm no deeper than the drainage reaches the surface as nothing. A volume allowance, not a pipe network — it does not know where the inlets are. 0 (the default) models no drainage.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">c966ca1a-01fd-474f-a660-aeda7670824a</item>
