                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Terrain samples per cell edge: 1 takes the cell centre, 2 or 3 averages an n×n grid inside it. Smooths a coarsely-meshed terrain. It does NOT recover sub-cell features — averaging a kerb into the cell mean is precisely how it disappears, which is what Breaklines are for.</item>
