            <chunk name="Object" index="11">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">2c6e6b5c-ddd1-4652-90d4-7ca9fe123f6e</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Description</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Purpose: Where water can pond on a graded site, and which way it runs.
Fidelity: Experimental - surface routing only, no pipes; the IDF coefficients are placeholders.
Method: Stormwater Grid rasterises the terrain at 1 m; Fast mode computes terrain analytics, Full mode solves shallow-water depths.
Result: A depression-capacity mesh and runoff flowlines up to 240 m, coloured by contributing area.
Needs: Nothing to install; runs inside Rhino. Runtime: seconds to minutes, Full mode the slower.
Edit: Terrain surface; real IDF coefficients a, b, c in Design Storm; connect Land Cover Runoff.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="5">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
