                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Site Context</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="10">
                    <item name="ClayLook" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">One click from a location to the site's context: buildings with heights, bare-earth terrain, tree crowns, land-cover ground zones with their roughness, and the inlet z0 per wind direction — fetched in the background from open data and placed in a local frame centred on the location (Rhino model units). Sources: OpenStreetMap buildings (ODbL; height from the height tag or building:levels x 3 m, else the Fallback Height — never guessed silently: every building's height KIND is in the report), GEDTM30 bare-earth DTM (CC BY 4.0), the Meta/WRI 1 m canopy height map plus OSM street trees (CC BY 4.0 / ODbL), and ESA WorldCover 2021 (CC BY 4.0). Buildings come from GlobalBuildingAtlas LoD1 (TUM, CC BY-NC 4.0 — heights PREDICTED by a model, every one labelled so) or from OpenStreetMap (ODbL — the height tag or building:levels x 3 m, else the Fallback Height), chosen on Building Source. Results are cached on disk, so a reopened document shows its context without a new fetch; pressing Fetch again, or Refresh from the sources on the right-click menu, downloads anew.

Version 1.21.0.827</item>
                    <item name="FetchLayerBuildings" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                    <item name="FetchLayerLandCover" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                    <item name="FetchLayerTerrain" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                    <item name="FetchLayerTrees" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
