                    <chunk name="param_input" index="7">
                      <items count="9">
                        <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Where the buildings come from. Global Building Atlas: LoD1 footprints worldwide with heights PREDICTED by a model (RMSE 1.5-8.9 m; TUM, CC BY-NC 4.0 — non-commercial use), read straight from the published tiles. OpenStreetMap: mapped footprints with the height tag or building:levels x 3 m, else the Fallback Height (ODbL; via the public Overpass mirrors, which can queue for minutes). Overture Maps: the newest release's building footprints (conflated from OpenStreetMap, Microsoft ML Buildings, Esri Community Maps, Google Open Buildings and others), with the height it states or num_floors x 3 m, else the Fallback Height - many buildings carry neither, so check Height Sources (ODbL-1.0 for the theme; the contributing datasets keep their own terms, Esri and Google CC BY 4.0; credit: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Overture Maps Foundation), read straight from the published files. The height KIND of every building is on its mesh and in the report.</item>
                        <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">de330930-6389-47a9-9b14-68b1592aacf8</item>
